      "id": 219419,
      "name": "Kratos13",
      "username": "Kratos13",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/65b543/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-06-27T02:06:50.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thanks Powerhound. &nbsp;Your explanation makes sense from a rules point of view. &nbsp;For the sake of consistency, though, I do wish the wording was the same as Apprentice Poisoner (“... it first deals...”). &nbsp;Literally EVERY other environment target card in the game uses “this card” or “it” so when the Wagon didn’t have this wording, my first thought was “why is this? - is this supposed to work differently than other environment targets?”.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Anyway, thanks again.</p>",
